{"kind":"request","text":"ARC-1 pre-code cohort proposal under b188f9e7, at main 5b342ee9. No source or execution. I read the complete ruling, source note commit 4a511674eb on builder/arc1-staged-design-20261114, and measurement a737a945 at fixture head 249f8f36. This replaces the staged-provider direction. No provider staging, cursor, paged publication or larger cap enters ARC-1. Build waits for AE-1.\n\nThe proposed cohort is the intersection of the following conditions, not their independent maxima. Let R be the complete replay-scope base, C the number of public copy descriptors including required foreign genesis copies, and Q the conservative total cost of classifying and completing exactly this entry under its current archive context. Q must count every repeated read, validation, source preparation, privacy check, publication step and confirmation. A measurement of one entry or source supplies no discount.\n\n1. Exactly one next entry is selected, either genesis bootstrap or immediately after an existing current-layout confirmed receipt. Its own canonical bytes are at most the configured bounds.entryBytes, currently 262144; each definition is at most bounds.definitionBytes, currently 262144. Source: packages/contract/src/bounds.ts:87,109-112 (usesPerEntry128, derivedEffects256 are kernel maxima, not archive promises). No whole old-prefix migration is included in a claimed one-entry proof. Existing migration behavior remains a separate supported archive path, not evidence that this entry fits.\n\n2. The root and every required foreign/declaration dependency must have an existing reviewed archive policy, complete exact lineage and complete privacy support. packages/scope/src/archive-privacy.ts:18-34 classifies every selected position and foreign use; archive-inventory.ts:79-95 validates policy, input kinds and metadata before payload selection. Passing a size/count predicate grants no export authority. Unknown support retains its existing refusal; it does not become a cheap supported cohort.\n\n3. Every local entry and required foreign copy has at most 64 effects. This follows OWNER_LIMIT=65 in packages/scope/src/archive-entry-metadata.ts:36,83-85 and the existing forecastArchiveEntryPrivacy refusal in archive-entry-privacy-cost.ts:23-33. Static witness constant: MAX_ARCHIVE_EFFECTS=OWNER_LIMIT-1, tied to that forecast by boundary cases. Kernel derivedEffects256 does not raise it.\n\n4. Distinct source identities fit ARCHIVE_SOURCE_PINS=64 (archive-source-pins.ts:15,43-45; archive-source-window.ts:26,47,61). The resulting publication must also satisfy R\u003e=1 and R+C\u003c=64, from archive-finish-cost.ts:51-58. This is a stricter copy constraint than saying uses\u003c=128. journal-selection.ts:17,98-100 independently bounds manifest foreignSources by64. Static constants follow those existing caps; no fixed claim of63 uses is valid because R and required genesis copies consume the same allowance.\n\n5. Every selected retained definition, entry, birth, rule, snapshot or value must have an authoritative measured size before any body read, with 0\u003csize\u003c=RETAINED_INPUT_BYTES=1048576 (contract/src/read.ts:43; archive-retained.ts:124,129-133). Size alone grants no admission. Each request, repeated read and cold/decode/hash charge belongs in Q: archive-retained.ts:22-44,112-114,145-170. There is no kernel bound on the whole rule row. A rule row above1MiB is outside this cohort even if Native admitted it; many individually small rows can also fall outside Q. I will not infer a total retained-byte guarantee from entryBytes or the wider CDF residency cap.\n\n6. Manifest and publication fit their actual existing serialization limits: JOURNAL_SELECTION_BYTES=1048576 (git/src/journal-selection-cost.ts:6); ARCHIVE_ROW_MANIFEST_BYTES=1048576, ARCHIVE_ROW_BYTES=2113536 and confirmed row bound32768 (scope/src/archive-row-cost.ts:6-11). The current finish additionally requires replayScopes\u003c=64 and newRetained\u003c=512 (archive-row-cost.ts:60-67). The exact predicted pending-row byte count must fit, using archivePendingRowBytesUpper at37-39; independent1MiB manifest and1MiB publication maxima do not imply that their combined row fits.\n\n7. The complete outgoing object set, including required parent objects and Git layout output, satisfies objects\u003c=8192 and bytes\u003c=min(provider maximum,8388608). Source: archive-transfer-cost.ts:6-7,23-31; driver.ts:99. Copies alone are not the transfer size. Journal layout must independently fit objects8192, trees2048, files8192, names32768, depth64, objectBytes8388608 and outputWork67108864 (git/src/journal-work.ts:29-37). Use the current journal selection/body/patch/append/commit forecasts, not a byte-only estimate.\n\n8. Q fits ALL original ArchiveBudget coordinates: entries\u003c=4096, attempts\u003c=512, nodes\u003c=64, calls\u003c=16384, metadata\u003c=4194304, inputWork\u003c=67108864 (archive-budget.ts:6). The algorithm selects one local entry, but every actual debit in each coordinate still counts. The deadline remains30 seconds (same file:7,43-49); static work fit promises no immunity to provider outage or timeout. Such transients retain their existing retry behavior.\n\nQ must include the actual source sizes and declaration sizes, with cold source preparation charges128*birth UTF-16 units and96*declaration units, plus the nonalias native fallback when required (archive-source-pins.ts:49-85). It must include prefix pin/frame/classification fees (archive-inventory-cost.ts:9-19,48-59), local body work32*entryBytes and each retained read forecast. It must include all components summed at archive-finish-cost.ts:88-99: setup, inventory, input, publication, selection reservation/serialization, body, patch, commit, append edges, append, transfer, rows and frontier. It must also include driver opening/target/provider/read-back/credential/revocation/closing work that those helpers expressly exclude. No cheap exploratory scout or prebuilt policy map supplies credit to the real pass.\n\nAE-1 proof dependency: owner act3a32a391 says installed-policy preparation becomes a bounded async operation before provider/export work. Its costs do not exist yet. Consequently the eight conditions define an exact proposed shape, but I cannot honestly certify a numeric largest member or complete sufficient Q today. The build must first enumerate AE-1's final charged setup vector and close every excluded cost above. A static test imports the real caps and cost functions, sums the complete worst-case vectors, and checks the inequalities. Any change to a cap/charge must break the corresponding boundary witness. Until that test and largest member exist, this is a proposal, not a proved one-pass guarantee.\n\nNamed stop: entry-outside-archive-cohort. A false structural bound or complete cost inequality permanently stops this scope at the exact local entry position/hash. No payload bytes, labels, arbitrary strings or retained bodies enter the stop record or logs. Reserve its finite local persistence cost before classification so an exhausted planner cannot lose the terminal result. Provider absence, unreadable policy/source, malformed state and timeout are not proof of outside-cohort size and retain their separate existing failures.\n\nThe preflight must run before ANY provider call for this entry, including fresh-row provider.format at archive-driver.ts:214-225, not merely before mint/sendArchive. AE-1 owns authenticated policy/target discovery; ARC-1 owns the complete local/foreign footprint check after those proofs and before provider I/O. If it discovers that the entry is outside the cohort, provider call counts for that entry are zero.\n\nFresh-row persistence needs an explicit change: ArchiveRows.stop at archive-row.ts:313-317 requires an existing row, but today that row's format comes from provider.format. I propose an ArchiveRows-owned provider-independent terminal record containing only full local scope, position/hash and named reason, checked before every pass. It supplies neither a format nor a repository receipt. The same owner projects it as a stopped diagnostic without fabricating provider metadata. It cannot use the existing restart path, which only admits stopped reasons limit/foreign-source-unavailable (archive-row.ts:54-57). No source change happens before acceptance.\n\nA person sees state=stopped and reason=entry-outside-archive-cohort in the existing secret-free archive-pass-diagnostic-v1 and archive-row-diagnostic-v1 operator tail. Add the reason to both allowlists: archive-driver.ts:466,489-494 and archive-operator.ts:12,83-87,97-114. object.ts:420-433 emits the row diagnostic at activation; the pass emits the stop when it happens. Current code has no general public archive-status route. docs/operate-a-service.md must state the exact cohort, how to read this operator diagnostic, the stopped entry, and that later entries of the scope cannot archive under this rule. Do not promise a UI or CLI surface that does not exist.\n\nFloors remain based solely on ArchiveRows.confirmed after exact provider read-back (driver.ts:448,499-505; floor-writer.ts:24-32,51-53). The stop contributes no receipt or coverage. The old confirmed prefix remains usable; a floor cannot cross the stopped entry.\n\nWitnesses after AE-1: (a) the largest member of the FINAL statically proved complete cohort confirms in one original-budget pass, including actual provider checks and full replay; boundary values come from the imported caps; (b) the unchanged a737a945 fixture stops permanently with the named reason, zero provider calls/payload, unchanged confirmation and floor-ahead at the blocked entry. That fixture's128 later copies plus required genesis already violate R+C\u003c=64 even before the work inequality, so it needs no inflated cap or repeated measurement.\n\nDecisions requested: accept this intersection and provider-independent named-stop shape; confirm ordinary transient provider/time failures remain retries rather than terminal cohort failures; and permit the final numerical Q/largest-member act immediately after AE-1's source contracts settle, before ARC-1 source. If you require a fully numeric sufficient cohort now, the missing AE-1 cost vector is the exact blocker. I will not replace it with an invented number.","body":{"conditions":"Accept or amend the ARC-1 cohort and named-stop proposal; decide whether to finalize the complete numerical cost inequalities after AE-1 before ARC-1 code, since AE-1 preparation costs do not yet exist.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3a32a3915d01caa2a58ef832c5ee0b1a86b10e49, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b188f9e7e742f08ed16ee476f002a51d8412410a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}